<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><rss xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" version="2.0"><channel><title>World News, Today World News, Latest International News, World Breaking News, Trending News of World - Times of India</title><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world</link><description>World News Today: Read the latest world news headlines, Current International breaking news world wide. In depth analysis and top news headlines world wide.</description><language>en-gb</language><lastBuildDate>2026-09-24T19:41:52+05:30</lastBuildDate><atom:link type="application/rss+xml" rel="self" href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/rssfeeds/296589292.cms"/><copyright>Copyright:(C) Thu, 24 Sep 2026 19:41:52 IST Bennett Coleman &amp; Co. Ltd, http://in.indiatimes.com/policyterms/1554651.cms</copyright><docs>http://syndication.indiatimes.com/</docs><image><title>World News, Today World News, Latest International News, World Breaking News, Trending News of World - Times of India</title><url>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/507610.cms</url><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world</link></image><item><title><![CDATA[Minnesota girl, 12, wins $10Kprize for her global anti-hate campaign]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134464053.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Natalie Flaherty, a 12-year-old from Minnesota, received the Gloria Barron Prize for her initiative against hate. She started her campaign, 'I Stand with Anne', by distributing bracelets that promote kindness. Flaherty's project evolved into a nationwide movement, reaching all 50 states and beyond. She plans to use her prize money to continue her advocacy and educational work on hate.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/meet-natalie-flaherty-the-minnesota-girl-who-turned-a-2023-halloween-idea-into-an-anti-hate-campaign-distributing-100000-bracelets-across-50-countries-now-the-12-year-old-has-won-a-10000-national-young-hero-prize/articleshow/134464053.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/meet-natalie-flaherty-the-minnesota-girl-who-turned-a-2023-halloween-idea-into-an-anti-hate-campaign-distributing-100000-bracelets-across-50-countries-now-the-12-year-old-has-won-a-10000-national-young-hero-prize/articleshow/134464053.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-24T19:11:30+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134464072,imgsize-98946.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[In 2000, California packed 662,700 shredded waste tires beneath an I-880 on-ramp; they cut...]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134462701.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Engineers faced challenges while upgrading a highway interchange in Milpitas due to unstable bay mud. They opted to use shredded waste tires as lightweight fill to prevent ground settlement. This choice reduced weight on the soft soil by 40 percent and saved significant project costs. Over two decades, the infrastructure has shown no maintenance issues or structural damage.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2000-california-packed-662700-shredded-waste-tires-beneath-an-i-880-on-ramp-they-cut-foundation-stress-40-saved-477000-and-calrecycle-later-reported-22-years-without-repairs-or-issues/articleshow/134462701.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2000-california-packed-662700-shredded-waste-tires-beneath-an-i-880-on-ramp-they-cut-foundation-stress-40-saved-477000-and-calrecycle-later-reported-22-years-without-repairs-or-issues/articleshow/134462701.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-24T19:11:11+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134464076,imgsize-1372393.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Man lost lamp in cave in 1953; became a NASA scientist, found it 68 years later]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134463171.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/19-year-old-lost-his-lamp-in-an-australian-cave-in-1953-survived-three-days-became-a-nasa-scientist-68-years-later-students-found-the-lamp-still-hanging/articleshow/134463171.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/19-year-old-lost-his-lamp-in-an-australian-cave-in-1953-survived-three-days-became-a-nasa-scientist-68-years-later-students-found-the-lamp-still-hanging/articleshow/134463171.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-24T18:53:50+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134463681,imgsize-1515208.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Tech industry group urges Trump administration to drop $103,265 H-1B fee proposal, asks how Silicon Valley will hire top talents]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134463162.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/tech-industry-group-urges-trump-administration-to-drop-103265-h-1b-fee-proposal-asks-how-silicon-valley-will-hire-top-talents/articleshow/134463162.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/tech-industry-group-urges-trump-administration-to-drop-103265-h-1b-fee-proposal-asks-how-silicon-valley-will-hire-top-talents/articleshow/134463162.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-24T18:35:08+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134463336,imgsize-49340.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[An English artist paid £2,090 for a painting listed only as ‘in the style of’ Helen McNicoll]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134461980.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[David Taylor made an astonishing find at a UK auction when he acquired an oil painting incorrectly attributed to Helen McNicoll for just £2,090. After expert examination, it was confirmed to be McNicoll's masterpiece, The Bean Harvest, appraised at £300,000. Canadian collector Pierre Lassonde later purchased the artwork for £174,000, ensuring its return to public viewing after a century, highlighting the often-hidden treasures lurking in regional auction houses.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/an-english-artist-paid-2090-for-a-painting-listed-only-as-in-the-style-of-helen-mcnicoll-experts-later-proved-it-was-her-long-lost-bean-harvest-valued-at-300000-and-sold-for-174000/articleshow/134461980.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/an-english-artist-paid-2090-for-a-painting-listed-only-as-in-the-style-of-helen-mcnicoll-experts-later-proved-it-was-her-long-lost-bean-harvest-valued-at-300000-and-sold-for-174000/articleshow/134461980.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-24T18:04:32+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134462524,imgsize-1618707.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[White House bars Politico reporter again despite judge's access order]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134462352.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/white-house-bars-politico-reporter-again-despite-judges-access-order/articleshow/134462352.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/white-house-bars-politico-reporter-again-despite-judges-access-order/articleshow/134462352.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-24T18:00:30+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Abhishek Mishra</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134462414,imgsize-1564968.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Meet Lucas Rojas, 16, who turned one inclusive kickball game into a six-team league with 40+ players]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134460054.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Lucas Rojas launched LINKball, a vibrant kickball league designed to unite students with special needs and enthusiastic volunteers. Starting from a charity match, this initiative blossomed into a well-organized league of six teams. Acknowledging his impactful work, Rojas was awarded the $10,000 Gloria Barron Prize. Each season sees over 40 players and 60 volunteers engaging in the program, promoting inclusivity and teamwork through the joy of sports.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/meet-lucas-rojas-the-16-year-old-miami-student-who-turned-one-inclusive-kickball-game-into-a-six-team-league-with-40-players-and-60-teen-volunteers-then-won-a-10000-national-young-hero-prize/articleshow/134460054.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/meet-lucas-rojas-the-16-year-old-miami-student-who-turned-one-inclusive-kickball-game-into-a-six-team-league-with-40-players-and-60-teen-volunteers-then-won-a-10000-national-young-hero-prize/articleshow/134460054.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-24T18:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134460162,imgsize-1819102.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Seattle’s 'Inconvenience Store': Former 7-Eleven sells tangled USBs, fake corn dogs and more]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134461582.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/seattles-inconvenience-store-a-former-7-eleven-reopened-as-an-art-shop-selling-pre-tangled-usb-cables-a-landline-iphone-fake-corn-dogs-and-useless-everyday-items/articleshow/134461582.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/seattles-inconvenience-store-a-former-7-eleven-reopened-as-an-art-shop-selling-pre-tangled-usb-cables-a-landline-iphone-fake-corn-dogs-and-useless-everyday-items/articleshow/134461582.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-24T17:38:54+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134461764,imgsize-777165.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Needs a miracle': Son of Israeli ambassador to US injured in West Bank ramming attack]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134460615.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/middle-east/needs-a-miracle-son-of-israeli-ambassador-to-us-injured-in-west-bank-ramming-attack/articleshow/134460615.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/middle-east/needs-a-miracle-son-of-israeli-ambassador-to-us-injured-in-west-bank-ramming-attack/articleshow/134460615.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-24T17:20:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Karan Manral</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134461476,imgsize-160416.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Michael Tilson Thomas’ 32-year home is now on sale for $9.85M]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134459906.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Michael Tilson Thomas’s residence in Pacific Heights is now on the market following his passing earlier this year. The mansion was a sanctuary for the musician and his husband Joshua Robison for nearly three decades. Built in 1906, the four-level home features a blend of architectural styles and modern amenities added over the years. Its spacious rooms hosted numerous distinguished guests from the music and architecture worlds.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/real-estate/news/in-1994-michael-tilson-thomas-paid-1-4-million-for-the-historic-1906-san-francisco-mansion-after-a-2012-remodel-and-32-years-as-his-home-the-7090-sq-ft-home-is-now-on-the-market-for-nearly-10-million/articleshow/134459906.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/real-estate/news/in-1994-michael-tilson-thomas-paid-1-4-million-for-the-historic-1906-san-francisco-mansion-after-a-2012-remodel-and-32-years-as-his-home-the-7090-sq-ft-home-is-now-on-the-market-for-nearly-10-million/articleshow/134459906.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-24T17:08:14+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Real Estate Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134460443,imgsize-391865.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[1 killed, 4 injured in knife attack at Benedictine abbey in Poland]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right: