on platform Flipcause collapsed owing 3,200 nonprofits $29 million]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134457447.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Flipcause, an Oakland-based donation platform, filed for bankruptcy in December 2025 after owing nearly $29 million to more than 3,200 nonprofits. Bankruptcy records showed the company paid $3.8 million to executives, relatives and related firms in the year before filing. Nonprofits later questioned Flipcause leadership over delayed donations and how company funds were managed.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2025-donation-platform-flipcause-collapsed-owing-more-than-3200-nonprofits-nearly-29-million-bankruptcy-records-later-showed-3-8-million-went-to-executives-relatives-and-related-firms-before-liquidation/articleshow/134457447.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2025-donation-platform-flipcause-collapsed-owing-more-than-3200-nonprofits-nearly-29-million-bankruptcy-records-later-showed-3-8-million-went-to-executives-relatives-and-related-firms-before-liquidation/articleshow/134457447.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-24T16:30:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134458602,imgsize-181556.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Wasp spider spotted in Cheshire for first time; Chester Zoo says species is moving north]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134457479.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[During a recent biodiversity assessment at Chester Zoo in Cheshire, researchers made an exciting discovery—'Wendy,' a wasp spider. This is the first time this species has been documented in the area, reflecting shifts in wildlife distribution due to climate change. As southern European habitats become less viable, wasp spiders are migrating northward, revealing the transformative effects of environmental changes on British ecosystems.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/wildlife/a-brightly-striped-wasp-spider-has-been-recorded-in-cheshire-for-the-first-time-chester-zoo-says-the-harmless-species-is-moving-north-as-warming-reshapes-where-british-wildlife-can-survive/articleshow/134457479.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/wildlife/a-brightly-striped-wasp-spider-has-been-recorded-in-cheshire-for-the-first-time-chester-zoo-says-the-harmless-species-is-moving-north-as-warming-reshapes-where-british-wildlife-can-survive/articleshow/134457479.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-24T15:30:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134457624,imgsize-2181510.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Florida businessman’s 4 beach lots to become public after a decade and multiple lawsuits]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134456624.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Michael Holderness bought four beachfront lots on Florida’s Siesta Key in 2016 and 2017, leading to years of disputes with Sarasota County over public access and development. Under a settlement, the county will receive the four lots and make them public beach property, while Holderness gets a nearby parcel valued at nearly $2.8 million, $500,000 and permission to build a 5,000-square-foot home.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2016-a-florida-businessman-began-buying-four-siesta-key-beach-lots-a-decade-and-multiple-lawsuits-later-a-county-land-swap-will-make-them-public-and-let-him-build-a-5000-sq-ft-home-on-another-parcel/articleshow/134456624.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2016-a-florida-businessman-began-buying-four-siesta-key-beach-lots-a-decade-and-multiple-lawsuits-later-a-county-land-swap-will-make-them-public-and-let-him-build-a-5000-sq-ft-home-on-another-parcel/articleshow/134456624.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-24T16:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134457289,imgsize-131330.cms"/></item></channel></rss>